## Context

Ticket 0270 settled the dyne design end-to-end (vision, composed-vs-
integrated arbitration, log home, no numbering, name). Phase 1 of the
migration path starts here. The PEP is documentation layer 1: written
before code, one numbered design choice per section (Choice / Rationale
/ Alternatives considered), and the arbiter of intent under the
three-scope authority model (spec normative for files, binary normative
for the spec's text, PEP arbitrates intent).

## Task

Write `pep-dyne-v1.md` beside `pep-erg-v1.md`, seeded from 0270's body.
Every settled choice gets its numbered section with the alternatives
that lost:

- state is the DAG (`git merge-base --is-ancestor` is the status field;
  no Status header, not even the file path carries state)
- one object = one plain-text file on the source branch
  (`tickets/merges/<branch>.dyne`); merging into main IS the archival act
  (rejected: dedicated refs, shared registry branch, MR-ticket fusion)
- erg's exact three-section grammar; log = one-liners, body = the
  discussion whose opening post is the description (comment #0)
- multi-writer merges via `merge=union` on `tickets/merges/*.dyne`; prose
  append-only by convention; `dyne check` fences the residual hazard
  (rejected: sibling `.log` file, custom merge driver)
- no archive numbering: the merge commit SHA is the permanent name;
  hooks receive `{sha}` (rejected: merge-time serial, safe but unneeded)
- composed on spec and behavior, one codebase two specs (the 0270
  comparison table is the pre-decision record to preserve)
- the composition seam: grammar by convention, references opaque,
  behavior via exec hooks (`.dynerc`)
- the name: dyne, the CGS unit of force -- erg = dyne x cm; standalone
  binary mirroring erg (rejected: git-mr/git mr, bid, darn)
- the seven invariants and the infrastructure-class security posture
  carried over from erg

## Exit criteria

- [ ] pep-dyne-v1.md merged, covering every settled choice of 0270 with
      its rationale and rejected alternatives
- [ ] the three-scope authority model stated in the PEP itself

## Author design amendment (2026-10-15)

Read `docs/dyne-review-contract.md` as the current amendment to 0270.
It supersedes the earlier root merges/ placement: use tickets/merges/,
with evidence under tickets/reviews/. Keep the Go/static/shared-codebase
plan and independent commands; no new path configuration or erg dependency.
The Dyne body carries the evolving plan; Hunt owns it and gaze executes it.
Preserve immutable per-pass requests/results and revision-bound evidence.
Open reuse, stop, concurrency and recovery questions are recorded for author
discussion, not silently settled. Follow the delivery phases in that document;
this ticket remains open and no implementation is claimed.
